A Python list is a built-in data structure which is used to store multiple values. It can contain different types of data such as 
integers, strings, and floats in the same list.Lists are flexible and easy to use where as a NumPy array is provided by the NumPy 
library and is mainly used for numerical calculations. It usually stores elements of the same data type and performs
mathematical operations much faster than Python lists.

Python lists use more memory and often require loops to perform calculations. In contrast, NumPy arrays use less memory and support direct element-wise operations, making them more
efficient for scientific and mathematical work.
